name light-latex-make
category Package
revision 60558
shortdesc llmk: A build tool for LaTeX documents
longdesc Light LaTeX Make (llmk) is yet another build tool specific for
longdesc LaTeX documents. Its aim is to provide a simple way to specify
longdesc a workflow of processing LaTeX documents and encourage people
longdesc to always explicitly show the right workflow for each document.
longdesc The main features of llmk are all about the above purpose.
longdesc First, you can describe the workflows either in an external
longdesc file llmk.toml or in a LaTeX document source in the form of
longdesc magic comments. Further, multiple magic comment formats can be
longdesc used. Second, it is fully cross-platform. The only requirement
longdesc of the program is the texlua command; llmk provides a uniform
longdesc way to describe the workflows available for nearly all TeX
longdesc environments. Third, it behaves exactly the same in any
longdesc environment. At this point, llmk intentionally does not provide
longdesc any method for user configuration. Therefore one can guarantee
longdesc that for a LaTeX document with an llmk setup, the process of
longdesc typesetting the document will be reproduced in any TeX
longdesc environment with the program.
depend light-latex-make.ARCH
containersize 10568
